{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nClosing a ticket can freeze every other agent's writes to the tickets store for minutes. The\nclose's post-write tail calls `_compact_on_close` (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:92`),\nwhich runs compaction; `compact_txn._compact_locked` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:328`)\ntakes the ONE store write lock at `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:340` and holds it for the\nwhole fold — read, reduce, authorship ledger, snapshot write, retire renames, and the git\nadd/commit. Measured on this host: closing `271c-e88f-3220-4c9b` held `.ticket-write.lock.d`\nfrom 20:35:52 until its `ticket: COMPACT` commit (72ff0358f7) at 20:49:45 — 13m53s, one\ncontinuous hold. Three other closes the same hour held 2m27s, 2m27s, 2m41s. Concurrent agents\nthen burn their acquire budget and lose writes.\n\nTwo mechanisms make the hold long. (1) The whole fold is inside the lock even though only the\nsnapshot write, the retire renames and the commit mutate anything. (2) Inside that lock every\ngit call goes through `compact_txn._git` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:41`) ->\n`gitutil.run_git_write` (`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:472`) -> `_with_index_lock_retry`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:339`), which opens with `_store_git_op_lock`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:365`) — a SECOND per-store advisory flock. Its budgets stack\ninside the held store lock: `_STORE_GIT_LOCK_WAIT_S = 30.0`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:209`), `_INDEX_LOCK_ATTEMPTS = 10`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:125`), each attempt up to `_TRANSIENT_HEAD_ATTEMPTS = 3`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:418`) children bounded by `_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT = 120`\n(`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:468`). Nothing bounds the aggregate: `_compact_locked`'s\n`timeout=30, attempts=2` bounds only ACQUIRING the store lock, never HOLDING it. The 7084\nstand-aside probe (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:121`) cannot help the closing\nprocess, which released the lock ~3s earlier so the store always reads free. Raw git is not\nthe cost: on this tracker (54,931 tracked files) `git status --porcelain` runs in 0.185s.\n\n## Approach\nKeep compaction where it is — still on close, same trigger, same artifacts — and shrink the\nlock to the mutation only. Split `_compact_locked` into an unlocked PREPARE phase and a locked\nCOMMIT phase:\n\n- PREPARE (no store lock): `_parse_candidate_events`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:176`), horizon partition, `reduce_ticket`, the strip +\n  `_build_authorship_ledger`, and the status guard. All reads and pure computation.\n- COMMIT (store lock held): re-list the ticket dir and compare against the exact candidate\n  file set PREPARE folded. Any difference means an event landed under us, so the prepared\n  fold is stale — abort the pass cleanly (exit 0, nothing written) and log a WARNING naming\n  the ticket and the reason. Compaction is optional work and a skip is already a documented\n  no-op for correctness (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:92`: the events stay live\n  and the next compaction folds them), so aborting is the honest TOCTOU answer and never a\n  stale write. On a match: take `snapshot_ts` (`hlc.next_tick` writes, so it stays inside the\n  lock), build and atomically write the SNAPSHOT, `_retire_folded_sources`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:238`), drop the cache, `_commit_compaction`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:310`), release.\n\nThen bound the aggregate inside that new critical section. `run_git_write` already accepts a\nper-call `timeout` (`src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:476`), but the git-op-lock wait and the retry\nloop are not capped. Add an optional `deadline` (monotonic timestamp) threaded through\n`run_git_write` -> `_with_index_lock_retry` -> `_store_git_op_lock`: the git-op-lock wait stops\nat the earlier of its own 30s and the deadline, the retry loop stops once the deadline passes,\nand each child's watchdog is clamped to the remaining budget. Default `None` keeps every\nexisting caller bit-for-bit unchanged. The commit phase passes a deadline of\n`_LOCKED_GIT_BUDGET_S`, a module constant set to 30s to match `_STORE_GIT_LOCK_WAIT_S` — the\nlongest wait a peer holding the git-op lock can legitimately impose — and kept a named\nconstant so the threshold can be tuned without touching call sites.\n\nOn expiry the commit phase stops, logs a WARNING naming the ticket and the remaining budget,\nand releases the store lock. It does NOT reverse the retirement: by that point the SNAPSHOT is\natomically written and the sources are renamed to `*.retired`, which is a CONSISTENT state, not\na torn one — the SNAPSHOT-present short-circuit makes a re-compact a no-op and the next store\nwrite's commit picks up the staged tree, exactly the crash-mid-rename reasoning\n`_retire_folded_sources` already documents\n(`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:242`). Its reverse-rename stays reserved for an OSError\ninside the retirement loop itself, which is the only fault that leaves a partial retirement.\n\nThis fits because it changes only WHERE the lock brackets, not WHEN compaction runs; it reuses\nseams that exist (`run_git_write`'s timeout parameter, the optional-work contract) rather than\nadding machinery; and it restores the invariant `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` already assumes —\nthe store lock brackets a store mutation, not an unbounded wait on a second lock.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` — split `_compact_locked` into the unlocked prepare and\n  locked commit phases; add the TOCTOU re-check, the locked-phase git budget, and the two\n  stand-aside WARNING lines.\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py` — optional `deadline` on `_store_git_op_lock`,\n  `_with_index_lock_retry`, `run_git_write` (default `None` = today's behaviour).\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_lock_hold_barbet.py` — new regression tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: a normal compaction still folds — same SNAPSHOT content, same retired sources,\n  same `ticket: COMPACT <id>` commit as before the split.\n- Lock-hold: a background sampler polls `.ticket-write.lock.d` every 20ms across a compaction\n  whose prepare phase is instrumented; zero samples show the lock present during prepare.\n- TOCTOU: an event appended between prepare and the locked re-check aborts the pass with no\n  SNAPSHOT written, no source retired, the events still live, and a WARNING logged; a\n  following compaction folds them.\n- Budget: with a peer holding `.git/rebar-git-op.lock`, the commit phase gives up within its\n  budget and releases the store lock, leaving the consistent SNAPSHOT-written + sources-retired\n  state and a WARNING.\n- Failure path: an OSError inside the retirement loop still reverses every completed rename.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Compaction's expensive fold (parse, reduce, authorship ledger) runs with the store write\n      lock NOT held — a test whose 20ms sampler records zero lock-dir observations during the\n      prepare phase.\n- [ ] An event appended between prepare and the locked re-check aborts the pass cleanly — the\n      test asserts no SNAPSHOT file, no `.retired` source, exit 0, a logged WARNING, and that a\n      subsequent compaction folds the ticket.\n- [ ] The locked phase cannot wait unbounded on the nested git-op lock — with a peer holding\n      `.git/rebar-git-op.lock`, a test asserts the call returns, the store lock dir is gone, and\n      the ticket is left in the consistent SNAPSHOT-written + sources-retired state.\n- [ ] Compaction still runs on close and produces the same artifacts — a test asserts the\n      SNAPSHOT, the retired sources and the `ticket: COMPACT <id>` commit are unchanged.\n- [ ] `run_git_write`'s existing callers are unaffected — the new `deadline` parameter defaults\n      to `None` and the full local gate set plus CI's pytest tiers pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786594193599597001,"uuid":"5ba65b1d-b7b1-45f0-ba5a-7df669317d42"}